  'draft', 'foundation',
  'A 34-year-old woman presents to her GP with a 3-day history of a spreading, warm, tender area of erythema over her right shin, with associated mild fever. She reports that five years ago she developed an itchy rash and facial swelling within an hour of taking amoxicillin for a chest infection. She has no other known drug allergies and is otherwise well, with observations: temperature 37.8C, HR 88 bpm, BP 118/76 mmHg.',
